  "rawText": "Chicken Tortilla Soup\n\n1/2 a good sized onion\n1 bell pepper (red, orange, yellow, green - in order of preference)\n3/4 cup carrots\n1 medium zucchini\n6-8 cloves garlic\n1 (4 ounce) can chopped green chiles\n\n3 teaspoons chili powder\n2 teaspoons dried oregano\n1 teaspoon cumin\n4 teaspoons salt\n1/2 teaspoon seasoning salt\n1/4 teaspoon thyme\n1/4 teaspoon paprika\n1 teaspoon black pepper\n1 sazon tomato/cilantro packet\nDash cayenne\nShake the shit out of the Cholula bottle for like 5 seconds\n\n3 corn tortillas\n\n1 15 ounce can crushed or diced roasted tomatoes\n2 32 oz. boxes vegetable or chicken broth\n1 cup water\n1 can black beans\n1 can great northern beans\n1/2ish cup frozen corn\nReal big handful cilantro\nJuice of 2 limes\n\nSauté the veggies + a little salt/cumin in a couple glugs of olive oil over medium high. Add everything except beans and lime. Simmer covered for a few hours. Add beans and lime.",
  "recipeType": "meal"
}
